  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: F1b: land the F1 spec-review retry commit on the fixed base",
  "spec": "Respec of T-1376: its commit d36d4e1 (branch task/T-1376) was built on goal/T-1375 at e953e54, where main was red from PR 28's committed pool.toml (fixed by PR 29, ffae658). goal/T-1375 now points at ffae658. Cherry-pick d36d4e1 onto this task branch, run the gate, commit. Change code only if the cherry-pick conflicts or the gate is red on the new base; keep the T-1376 design exactly (bus_read T-1376 for the full spec: daemon retries a spec review whose children all failed, up to [daemon].respawn_max, then holds the task with spec_review_failed).",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1379"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_failed_spec_review_is_retried",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_spec_review_failures_hold_after_respawn_max",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_pending_spec_review_not_duplicated",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/<this task> exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/daemon.py",
    "tests/test_daemon.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1381",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "The diff matches the T-1376 design: retry only when all spec_review children are failed or superseded, hold with spec_review_failed at respawn_max, and skip when a live child exists. It adds no new privilege or trust-boundary surface. clear_stage and respawn_max both exist and are used the same way elsewhere in daemon.py. The three named acceptance tests are present as unittest methods, and the gate is recorded as green on the first attempt. I did not run the tests myself.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/daemon.py",
        "line": 987,
        "issue": "Held-at-limit branch: if stamp() returns False (already stamped), the task is left un-notified and silently skipped every tick. This is benign and idempotent. The 'superseded' status is also counted as a failure toward respawn_max, which is a slight over-count but acceptable.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
